14.5,1956,54,91,24],[20199,24.4,1956,58,87,24],[20200,20.8,2020,60,91,22]],"links":[["Taos County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/new-mexico/taos-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 16 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years. In 2025, January to February came in at 47% of normal on the middle of the grids, and May to June came in at 184%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 25% of normal on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
